WASM DemoModeLevel: boot the real front end before the race (parity with native)

Same rationale as the native launcher (commit c631f33): the original reaches every
attract/race through Init_Front_End, whose LEV0 texture load fills texturespace
pages 20-25 (+ parts of 6-19) that race levels never overwrite; skipping it left
them zero (black sky-panorama wedges, texturespace 77.7% vs the reference --
100.00% with the FE boot). festate re-applied after: it captures the reference's
post-FE state. Without this the native and WASM builds diverge in texturespace.

--- a/dd2_runtime.c
+++ b/dd2_runtime.c
@@ -41,6 +41,17 @@
      Init_Overlays would skip its -0x10 tpage adjust -> overlay textures one VRAM page off. */
   *(int*)0x462fe8 = 0;
   { extern void dd2_apply_frontend_state(void); dd2_apply_frontend_state(); }  /* dd2_festate.c */
+  /* Boot the REAL front end exactly like the original (and tools/native_main.c): Init_Front_End
+     loads the LEV0 texture set into texturespace pages the race levels never overwrite
+     (pages 20-25 + parts of 6-19 were zero -> black sky-panorama wedges vs the reference) and
+     runs the FE init chain (fonts/sprites/objects). race_type/race_mode must be 0 first
+     (valid string-table index; else FUN_00450640 OOB). pal_flag + festate re-applied after:
+     festate IS the reference's post-FE state. */
+  *(int*)0x4673f4 = 0;  /* race_type */
+  *(int*)0x4673f8 = 0;  /* race_mode */
+  { extern void Init_Front_End(void); Init_Front_End(); }
+  *(int*)0x462fe8 = 0;
+  { extern void dd2_apply_frontend_state(void); dd2_apply_frontend_state(); }
   Setup_Pad(1);
   *(int*)0x93de1c=*(int*)0x4673f4; *(int*)0x93de18=*(int*)0x4673f8;
   /* demo_mode=1 (recorded-pad attract) by default; DD2_LIVE -> 0 = live keyboard input.
